    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n12029" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">currīlis</span></b> , e, adj.
		currus, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>of</i> or <i>for a chariot</i> (late
			Lat.): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">praesepia equorum currilium,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Vulg. 3
					Reg. 4, 26</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">certamina,</span>”
				<i>chariot-races</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Ambros. Cant. Cantic. 7, 12</span></i>
			: currilis equus, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σὺν ἅρματι
				ἀγωνιζόμενος ἵππος</span>, Gloss. Labb.; cf. also
			curulis.</div>
